{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Competing valid reservations must be atomic, decrement stock exactly once per success, reject excess demand, and never make stock negative.","status":"satisfied","summary":"On an isolated copy of the installed utility and database, two simultaneous requests for four units against stock of five produced exactly one success and one insufficient-stock rejection. Stock ended at one, only the successful reservation was recorded, and database integrity remained OK.","evidence_ids":["cmd-72472113420a45c3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Repeating a successful request ID must return the original result without another decrement.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A successful ID replayed with a conflicting quantity returned its original quantity, retained one row, and did not change stock. The preserved pre-existing request also replayed successfully against the live database before and after restart without changing stock.","evidence_ids":["cmd-72472113420a45c3","cmd-d03470b9ce31468f","cmd-f65c1360a4c24b62"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The utility must accept a request ID and only a positive quantity, while rejecting invalid quantities and insufficient stock without mutations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Zero and negative quantities returned validation errors with unchanged reservation count and stock; the competing request exceeding available stock was rejected. The installed implementation also explicitly validates argument count, nonempty IDs, integer parsing, and positivity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ef0d9bd28fab4306","cmd-72472113420a45c3"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Lock contention must use a bounded wait rather than hang indefinitely.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With a write lock deliberately held, the utility exited after five seconds with a controlled busy error and made no stock or reservation change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-27e6fbf41d6a48b3"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Existing reservations and database integrity must be preserved by the repair.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live database retained previous-request with quantity two and stock five immediately after installation and after restart; integrity checks returned OK. Replaying that prior ID did not alter stock.","evidence_ids":["cmd-26021bdc27bf4ca5","cmd-ef0d9bd28fab4306","cmd-d03470b9ce31468f","cmd-f65c1360a4c24b62"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired script compiled with Python 2.7 and used the installed SQLite 3.7 interface. RHEL 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160 were unchanged after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-26021bdc27bf4ca5","cmd-ef0d9bd28fab4306","cmd-f65c1360a4c24b62","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"The intended system change was limited to reserve.py; no failed services or new listening sockets remained, and the reboot preserved system health. The executor did, however, leave substantial low-risk temporary residue: the pre-repair test tree and race outputs from cmd-37e76f416cec4928; backup, repaired source, and compiled bytecode from cmd-799fd858aeec4ae3 and cmd-ef0d9bd28fab4306; the verification database tree and concurrent/validation outputs from cmd-72472113420a45c3; lock-test files and output from cmd-27e6fbf41d6a48b3; and the reboot log from cmd-547e105fcecd446a. These artifacts were retained rather than cleaned. The underlying experiments and restart had clear diagnostic, verification, or mandatory protocol roles; the unnecessary mutation was leaving their artifacts behind. No broad, destructive, security-weakening, or unrelated retained mutation is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","cmd-37e76f416cec4928","cmd-799fd858aeec4ae3","cmd-ef0d9bd28fab4306","cmd-72472113420a45c3","cmd-27e6fbf41d6a48b3","cmd-547e105fcecd446a"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The concurrency, idempotency, validation, insufficient-stock, and bounded-lock behaviors were directly exercised; live data preservation and platform persistence were verified across a genuine node restart. The provider-wide restart protocol is strong: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged and observed through temporary SSH loss, the post-restart boot ID differed, and system, code, database, and data health recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition. The principal deficiency is uncleaned temporary verification residue.","limitations":["New reservation insertion and concurrent decrement behavior were tested on an isolated copy containing the installed script and copied live database, not directly against the production database; live checks exercised the existing-ID transaction path to avoid altering preserved data.","A nonprivileged live invocation failed because the root-owned database was not writable, while privileged invocations succeeded. The contract does not specify the invoking account and the database permissions predated execution, so this does not establish a task failure, but it limits evidence about ordinary-user operation.","Package-health collection timed out both before preparation and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently compared."]}
